            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0141" n="39" xml:id="pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee (Arms)/163:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Delegate</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-28T18:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>490. Your 1027, March 27, 11 a.m. We feel strongly that the Committees should
                    write a single text with reservations rather than writing a text in two
                    columns.</p>
                <p>In view of the general political situation we incline to favor the idea of
                    continuing to work in private. We feel that if reservations of importance are
                    entered by only one or two States, the pressure of public opinion to induce them
                    to withdraw those reservations would be just as effective as public opinion
                    mobilized at this time to prevent their insertion and the attendant dangers of
                    an acrimonious public debate would be avoided.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
